{"event": "tool_call", "t": 1795226391.174, "name": "report", "arguments": {"verdict": "escalate", "root_cause": {"category": "config", "model": "rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed", "summary": "The waterfall model is built and its numbers reconcile to the marketing spend source. It lands in main_analytics.rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed rather than analytics.rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed, because the project profile's target schema is 'main' and the custom generate_schema_name macro prefixes it. The task needs the analytics schema, and that needs a profiles.yml change, which the edit tool blocks."}, "evidence": [{"kind": "lineage", "ref": "walk_lineage dim_fact_marketing_spend upstream", "finding": "Spend source is dim_fact_marketing_spend (built from stg_fact_marketing_spend, which reads source enterprise_db.FACT_MARKETING_SPEND). It has 1000 rows, 30 campaign_ids, no null or negative spend or revenue."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "dim_fact_marketing_spend campaign/channel profile", "finding": "Every campaign spans several channel_key values (7 to 10). The model picks the channel_key with the highest total spend per campaign, as the task requires."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "dim_fact_marketing_spend duplicates", "finding": "Six campaign-days have two rows each, with different channel_keys. The model sums them into one campaign-day row."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "main_analytics.rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed reconciliation", "finding": "994 rows, 30 campaigns, 0 duplicate (campaign_id, days_since_cohort), 30 cohort rows at day 0, 0 negative values. Last cumulative spend 5048804.17 equals source spend 5048804.17. Last cumulative revenue 10400419.59 equals source revenue 10400419.59."}, {"kind": "diff", "ref": "profiles.yml", "finding": "Target dev has no schema set, so the target schema is main. edit_model refused to change profiles.yml, so I could not set schema analytics there."}], "changes": [{"path": "models/marts/marketing/rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed.sql", "summary": "New model. Aggregates spend and revenue per campaign and day, keeps the highest-spend channel_key per campaign, builds the cumulative waterfall from the cohort date, and rounds currency to 2 dp and payback_ratio to 4 dp. Built and verified with run_dbt. It is materialised as a table with schema 'analytics', which currently resolves to main_analytics."}], "confidence": "medium"}, "duration_s": 0.0, "output_chars": 75, "is_error": false}
