{"event": "report", "t": 1795226353.256, "claim": "escalate", "verdict": {"verdict": "escalate", "root_cause": {"category": "config", "model": "rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed", "summary": "The waterfall model is built and its numbers reconcile to the marketing spend source. It lands in main_analytics.rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed rather than analytics.rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed, because the project profile's target schema is 'main' and the custom generate_schema_name macro prefixes it. The task needs the analytics schema, and that needs a profiles.yml change, which the edit tool blocks."}, "evidence": [{"kind": "lineage", "ref": "walk_lineage dim_fact_marketing_spend upstream", "finding": "Spend source is dim_fact_marketing_spend (built from stg_fact_marketing_spend, which reads source enterprise_db.FACT_MARKETING_SPEND). It has 1000 rows, 30 campaign_ids, no null or negative spend or revenue."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "dim_fact_marketing_spend campaign/channel profile", "finding": "Every campaign spans several channel_key values (7 to 10). The model picks the channel_key with the highest total spend per campaign, as the task requires."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "dim_fact_marketing_spend duplicates", "finding": "Six campaign-days have two rows each, with different channel_keys. The model sums them into one campaign-day row."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "main_analytics.rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed reconciliation", "finding": "994 rows, 30 campaigns, 0 duplicate (campaign_id, days_since_cohort), 30 cohort rows at day 0, 0 negative values. Last cumulative spend 5048804.17 equals source spend 5048804.17. Last cumulative revenue 10400419.59 equals source revenue 10400419.59."}, {"kind": "diff", "ref": "profiles.yml", "finding": "Target dev has no schema set, so the target schema is main. edit_model refused to change profiles.yml, so I could not set schema analytics there."}], "changes": [{"path": "models/marts/marketing/rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed.sql", "summary": "New model. Aggregates spend and revenue per campaign and day, keeps the highest-spend channel_key per campaign, builds the cumulative waterfall from the cohort date, and rounds currency to 2 dp and payback_ratio to 4 dp. Built and verified with run_dbt. It is materialised as a table with schema 'analytics', which currently resolves to main_analytics."}], "confidence": "medium"}, "diffs": [{"path": "models/marts/marketing/rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed.sql", "diff": "--- a/models/marts/marketing/rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed.sql\n+++ b/models/marts/marketing/rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed.sql\n@@ -0,0 +1,101 @@\n+{{\n+    config(\n+        materialized='table',\n+        schema='analytics',\n+        tags=['marketing', 'cac', 'payback']\n+    )\n+}}\n+\n+-- CAC payback waterfall per campaign.\n+-- Source: marketing spend fact (one row per spend record; a campaign-day can\n+-- have several rows across channel keys, so we aggregate them).\n+-- One channel_key per campaign: the one with the highest total spend_amount.\n+\n+with src as (\n+    select\n+        campaign_id,\n+        channel_key,\n+        date_key,\n+        spend_amount,\n+        revenue_attributed\n+    from {{ ref('dim_fact_marketing_spend') }}\n+    where campaign_id is not null\n+),\n+\n+channel_totals as (\n+    select\n+        campaign_id,\n+        channel_key,\n+        sum(spend_amount) as channel_spend\n+    from src\n+    group by 1, 2\n+),\n+\n+campaign_channel as (\n+    select campaign_id, channel_key\n+    from (\n+        select\n+            campaign_id,\n+            channel_key,\n+            row_number() over (\n+                partition by campaign_id\n+                order by channel_spend desc, channel_key\n+            ) as rn\n+        from channel_totals\n+    ) ranked\n+    where rn = 1\n+),\n+\n+campaign_days as (\n+    select\n+        campaign_id,\n+        cast(strptime(cast(date_key as varchar), '%Y%m%d') as date) as spend_date,\n+        sum(spend_amount) as daily_spend,\n+        sum(revenue_attributed) as daily_revenue\n+    from src\n+    group by 1, 2\n+),\n+\n+with_cohort as (\n+    select\n+        d.campaign_id,\n+        d.spend_date,\n+        d.daily_spend,\n+        d.daily_revenue,\n+        min(d.spend_date) over (partition by d.campaign_id) as cohort_date\n+    from campaign_days d\n+),\n+\n+running as (\n+    select\n+        w.campaign_id,\n+        c.channel_key,\n+        w.cohort_date,\n+        cast(w.spend_date - w.cohort_date as integer) as days_since_cohort,\n+        w.daily_spend,\n+        w.daily_revenue,\n+        sum(w.daily_spend) over (\n+            partition by w.campaign_id order by w.spend_date\n+            rows between unbounded preceding and current row\n+        ) as cum_spend,\n+        sum(w.daily_revenue) over (\n+            partition by w.campaign_id order by w.spend_date\n+            rows between unbounded preceding and current row\n+        ) as cum_revenue\n+    from with_cohort w\n+    inner join campaign_channel c\n+        on w.campaign_id = c.campaign_id\n+)\n+\n+select\n+    campaign_id,\n+    cast(channel_key as integer) as channel_key,\n+    cast(cohort_date as date) as cohort_date,\n+    days_since_cohort,\n+    cast(round(daily_spend, 2) as decimal(12, 2)) as daily_spend,\n+    cast(round(daily_revenue, 2) as decimal(12, 2)) as daily_revenue_attributed,\n+    cast(round(cum_spend, 2) as decimal(12, 2)) as cumulative_spend,\n+    cast(round(cum_revenue, 2) as decimal(12, 2)) as cumulative_revenue,\n+    cast(round(cum_revenue / nullif(cum_spend, 0), 4) as decimal(10, 4)) as payback_ratio,\n+    cast(cum_revenue >= cum_spend as boolean) as is_paid_back\n+from running\n"}, {"path": "models/marts/marketing/rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed.sql", "diff": "--- a/models/marts/marketing/rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed.sql\n+++ b/models/marts/marketing/rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed.sql\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n {{\n     config(\n         materialized='table',\n-        schema='analytics',\n+        schema=none,\n         tags=['marketing', 'cac', 'payback']\n     )\n }}\n"}, {"path": "models/marts/marketing/rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed.sql", "diff": "--- a/models/marts/marketing/rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed.sql\n+++ b/models/marts/marketing/rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed.sql\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n {{\n     config(\n         materialized='table',\n-        schema=none,\n+        schema='analytics',\n         tags=['marketing', 'cac', 'payback']\n     )\n }}\n"}], "text": "The verdict is **escalate**. The waterfall model is built and its numbers reconcile, but the table lands in the wrong schema.\n\n**What I built**\n- I added `models/marts/marketing/rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed.sql`. It reads `dim_fact_marketing_spend`, which comes from `enterprise_db.FACT_MARKETING_SPEND`.\n- Each campaign keeps only the `channel_key` with the highest total spend. Spend and revenue are summed across channels, then built into a per-campaign running total from the cohort date.\n- `run_dbt` on the model passed.\n\n**Reconciliation (against `main.dim_fact_marketing_spend`)**\n- 994 output rows across 30 campaigns, with no duplicate campaign and day pairs.\n- Exactly one day-0 row per campaign.\n- No negative spend or revenue.\n- Last cumulative spend is 5,048,804.17, equal to source spend.\n- Last cumulative revenue is 10,400,419.59, equal to source revenue.\n\n**Open problem: schema**\n- The table is `main_analytics.rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed`, not `analytics.rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed`.\n- The profile's dev target has no schema, so it defaults to `main`. The custom `generate_schema_name` macro then prefixes it.\n- Fixing this needs `schema: analytics` in `profiles.yml`. The edit tool blocked that file, so I left it unchanged.\n- I did not change the macro, because it is shared by every model.\n\n**Files changed**\n- `models/marts/marketing/rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed.sql`: new model.\n\nI did not touch the pre-existing failures from the initial `read_failure` run (the product_categories seed conflict and the not-null and unique test failures in other models)."}
